    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by three high-efficiency starts that break the 60-point threshold. **Daulton Varsho** leads the way at 69.56, benefiting from a soft matchup against M\u00e1rquez and his 5.58 xERA. While **Varsho** faces a slight efficiency tax due to the opponent's ability to hold runners, his premium positioning in the order and the favorable SP skill gap make him our most reliable point-generator. Similarly, the duo of **Taylor Ward** (68.88) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) are in excellent spots against Lugo. Both hitters capitalize on a positive park factor and a weak-to-average SP skill set, which offsets the minor platoon drag and the risk posed by Lugo's SB-suppression tactics. **Jung Hoo Lee** rounds out the tier at 62.57, taking full advantage of a plus-platoon matchup against Lorenzen to bolster our overall consistency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench remains the exclusion of **Bryce Harper**, who sits at 50.42 despite his elite underlying xwOBA. The harsh reality of today\u2019s matchups is that **Harper** is forced to square off against the high-end skill of Skubal (2.69 xERA), creating a negative SP skill adjustment that drags his efficiency below that of **JJ Bleday** (53.63) and **Jonathan Aranda** (55.23). While we hate leaving a superstar like **Bryce Harper** on the pine, the optimizer prioritizes the path of least resistance against weaker arms like Lorenzen and Boyd. Meanwhile, **Drew Gilbert** (51.55) was the final cut; while he mirrors the platoon benefits enjoyed by **Luis Arraez** against Lorenzen, **Gilbert**\u2019s low spot in the order suppresses his counting stat upside too much to displace our current starters.\n\nManagers should monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** (52.07), who faces Seymour in a matchup where the SP skill deficit is mitigated by the park and the advantage of hitting third. We are also keeping a close eye on the stolen base profile of **Dylan Beavers**; while the matchup against Lugo suggests a lower probability of running, his speed remains a critical asset in our league-wide strategy. We are opting to bench **Ryan Waldschmidt** entirely (41.62) given the severe penalty for hitting in the nine-hole against Sheehan, ensuring we preserve our game caps for the high-floor production provided by **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Tyler Freeman**.",
